{"cluster_id": "C-2374", "topic": "Counter maintenance covers add precommit, remove precommit, remove", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B021-061"], "canonical_claim": "Counter maintenance covers add precommit, remove precommit, remove committed, promote, and set payload; `set_payload` changes only `snapshot_body_bytes` because the ref name and manifest reference used by removal encoding do not change.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-20-cas-ref-admits-incremental-budget-design.md#L121-L140"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2375", "topic": "recovery_in_progress already serializes same-table concurrent callers across the", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B022-012"], "canonical_claim": "`recovery_in_progress` already serializes same-table concurrent callers across the recovery window, so extending the retry loop does not change the recovery concurrency invariant.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-20-cas-table-load-stuck-asyncloader-design.md#layer-1"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2376", "topic": "submitBatch enqueues ordinary per-item mutation records atomically but", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B023-067"], "canonical_claim": "`submitBatch` enqueues ordinary per-item mutation records atomically but waits for all of the submitting group's items; concurrent items may join its flushes and existing same-ref and `WholeShard` carve rules remain unchanged.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-22-cas-batched-part-commit-v2-design.md#submission-groups"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2377", "topic": "When adding the next item's operations would exceed", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B023-070"], "canonical_claim": "When adding the next item's operations would exceed `ref_txn_max_ops`, the item and later unvalidated items are returned to the head of `pending` in order; the current flush proceeds without an exception.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-22-cas-batched-part-commit-v2-design.md#budget"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2378", "topic": "dropRefIfMatches must perform its read-and-remove condition inside one", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B023-093"], "canonical_claim": "`dropRefIfMatches` must perform its read-and-remove condition inside one `appendRefOps` builder, returning true only when the current committed binding equals the expected manifest.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-22-cas-parallel-write-path.md#task-2-exact-manifest-commit-outcome-droprefifmatches"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2379", "topic": "The ref-ledger carve is two-phase: a throwing plan", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B024-013"], "canonical_claim": "The ref-ledger carve is two-phase: a throwing plan scans `pending` and reserves all capacity without mutation, then a no-throw publish under the same `ref_queue_mutex` pops selected items and moves them into `owned_items`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-22-cas-writepath-stage1-internal-design.md#two-phase-carve"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2380", "topic": "The validation loop reserves final_ops and survivors before", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B024-015"], "canonical_claim": "The validation loop reserves `final_ops` and `survivors` before applying an item to `working`, and publishes `working` only after all accumulation operations that may throw have completed.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-22-cas-writepath-stage1-internal-design.md#two-phase-carve"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2381", "topic": "Each ref-ledger chunk is a complete commit boundary", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B024-017"], "canonical_claim": "Each ref-ledger chunk is a complete commit boundary: it allocates a real transaction id, encodes and PUTs the chunk, applies it to `rt->state`, updates tail counters and metrics, completes that chunk's survivors, wakes waiters, and schedules snapshot publication before reseeding the next chunk from live state.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-22-cas-writepath-stage1-internal-design.md#budget"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2382", "topic": "Recovery publication installs every RecoveryResult field atomically under", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B024-025"], "canonical_claim": "Recovery publication installs every `RecoveryResult` field atomically under `state_mutex`, sets `recovered` last, and notifies waiters only after state, cleanup markers, snapshot identity, tail accounting, budgets, stale-precommit state, and recovery-seal facts are complete.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-22-cas-writepath-stage1-internal-design.md#recovery-streaming"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2383", "topic": "For chunk commit, the candidate is built by", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B024-042", "B025-008"], "canonical_claim": "For chunk commit, the candidate is built by copying live state and applying the complete chunk with the real transaction id before PUT; after a committed PUT, the candidate is moved into `rt->state` under `state_mutex` and `DENY_ALLOCATIONS_IN_SCOPE`, then materialized outside the deny region.; `commitRefChunk` builds and applies a COW candidate before the ref-log PUT, so allocation failures occur before durability; the candidate is not materialized before the PUT because its shared COW base would force an O(n) rebuild per chunk.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-24-cas-publish-confirm-and-ref-lane-safety.md#L226-L315", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-23-cas-fetch-handoff-publish-confirm-design.md#no-throw-install"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2384", "topic": "The apply-pending marker transitions Clean \u2192 ApplyPending before", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B024-044"], "canonical_claim": "The apply-pending marker transitions `Clean \u2192 ApplyPending` before a durable PUT, returns to `Clean` after successful apply or proven non-durability, and becomes terminal `Poisoned` when apply throws after durability; only fresh recovery clears `Poisoned`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-23-cas-fetch-handoff-publish-confirm-design.md#poison"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2385", "topic": "An unresolved relink abort leaves the ref lane", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B024-055"], "canonical_claim": "An unresolved relink abort leaves the ref lane wedged until exact-GET resolution or remount; a landed abort PUT is applied before unwedging, while a never-landing PUT causes retry-later behavior and fail-long over-protection.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-23-cas-fetch-handoff-publish-confirm-design.md#relink-handle"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2386", "topic": "RefTableState::swap(RefTableState & other) noexcept is the sanctioned post-durable", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B025-009"], "canonical_claim": "`RefTableState::swap(RefTableState & other) noexcept` is the sanctioned post-durable installation operation, and member-wise swaps keep destruction of the old state outside the allocation-denied install region.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-24-cas-publish-confirm-and-ref-lane-safety.md#L251-L280"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2387", "topic": "Wedge resolution is a post-durable install: it must", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B025-012"], "canonical_claim": "Wedge resolution is a post-durable install: it must install the decoded transaction exactly once by noexcept swap, clear the wedge in the deny region, and swallow a later `materializeCommitted` failure so the same transaction is not re-applied.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-24-cas-publish-confirm-and-ref-lane-safety.md#L578-L629"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2388", "topic": "confirmExactRef answers whether ref_name in a namespace still", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B025-016"], "canonical_claim": "`confirmExactRef` answers whether `ref_name` in a namespace still names exactly `manifest_ref` in the writer's committed view, performs zero object-store I/O, and returns `Unknown` for cold, evicted, or recovering tables instead of recovering them.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-24-cas-publish-confirm-and-ref-lane-safety.md#L783-L837"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2389", "topic": "NoAttemptSent means both pre-attempt gates rejected before backend->putIfAbsent", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B025-034"], "canonical_claim": "`NoAttemptSent` means both pre-attempt gates rejected before `backend->putIfAbsent`; therefore `commitRefChunk` must not install a wedge, while a fence lost after an attempt (`FenceLostMidWay`) must still wedge.", "issue_ids": ["#37"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-24-cas-publish-confirm-and-ref-lane-safety.md#L1358-L1434"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2390", "topic": "Recovery rejects raw or compressed ref-log bodies over", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B025-045"], "canonical_claim": "Recovery rejects raw or compressed ref-log bodies over the configured cap with `CORRUPTED_DATA`; corruption is not classified as transient and is rethrown instead of triggering a relist.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-24-codex-stage1-reviews.md#round-2"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2391", "topic": "Current-build set_published_at ref-log encode, decode, and apply preserve", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B025-046"], "canonical_claim": "Current-build `set_published_at` ref-log encode, decode, and apply preserve the same ref name, expected manifest, and timestamp.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-24-codex-stage1-reviews.md#round-2"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2392", "topic": "The final recovery memory guards use decoded transaction", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B025-048"], "canonical_claim": "The final recovery memory guards use decoded transaction footprints and require both an upper bound near one transaction and a lower bound at least as large as the largest actual transaction, including an independent ledger recovery test.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-24-codex-stage1-reviews.md#verify-pass-2"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2393", "topic": "sealed_from is paired with newest_snapshot_id: recovery seals install", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B025-049"], "canonical_claim": "`sealed_from` is paired with `newest_snapshot_id`: recovery seals install both values, while later ordinary or removed snapshots adopt a null `sealed_from` and clear the predecessor seal binding.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-24-codex-stage1-reviews.md#verify-pass-2"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2394", "topic": "Under the every-attempt rule, an id is freed", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B027-017"], "canonical_claim": "Under the every-attempt rule, an id is freed only when nothing was sent or every sent attempt has its own conclusive rejection; a definite rejection after an ambiguous attempt keeps the namespace lane wedged.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-27-cas-ref-chain-complete-cut-design.md#invariants"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2395", "topic": "A fold seal has at most one ref-life", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B027-028"], "canonical_claim": "A fold seal has at most one ref-life row per `Live` or `Removing` catalog row in its cut; input rows whose opaque ids are absent from the cut are counted and dropped rather than admitted or used to force `DEFER`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-27-cas-ref-chain-complete-cut-design.md#invariants"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2396", "topic": "An immutable catalog cut is the decoded bytes", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B027-015", "B027-035", "B031-027"], "canonical_claim": "An immutable catalog cut is the decoded bytes and object token from one successful `GET cas/ref_catalog`, plus a reverse index built once from those bytes; a consumer must not patch or mix that index with a later catalog GET.; A complete catalog GET is treated as an atomic object-version cut, whereas a paginated LIST stitches separately fetched pages and is not an atomic universe observation; downstream protocol can close staleness after a cut, but cannot recover a namespace omitted from the universe listing. The catalog remains the authoritative namespace universe because a single token-CAS `GET` supplies one complete object-version cut, whereas stitched paginated `LIST` results need not represent any namespace set at one instant.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-31-stage-b-strategic-review-codex.md#verdict", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-27-cas-ref-chain-complete-cut-design.md#invariants", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-27-cas-ref-chain-complete-cut-design.md#problem"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2397", "topic": "RefAppendWedge carries {key, bytes, RefTxnId id, uint64_t admitted_fence_generation}", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-081", "B025-011", "B027-126"], "canonical_claim": "`RefAppendWedge` carries `{key, bytes, RefTxnId id, uint64_t admitted_fence_generation}` and enforces at most one in-flight PUT per namespace lane.; The ref-lane flush uses a per-table \"wedge\": at most one outstanding record per table holding the key and sealed bytes of a single conditional PUT whose outcome is unresolved. The next flush must resolve that exact key (via `resolveByExactGet`) before it may allocate a new transaction id, which is what realizes INV-14 (fail-closed on ambiguity) and prevents the ledger from ever silently creating a gap or double-publishing.; The unresolved ref-log wedge is preconstructed before the PUT so its exact `{id, key, bytes}` can be moved into runtime state without allocation after an ambiguous outcome.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/11-walkthrough.md#ref-write-protocol", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-24-cas-publish-confirm-and-ref-lane-safety.md#L486-L577", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-a-streams.md#task-4"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2398", "topic": "Manifest objects retain (namespace, mount-epoch, build-sequence) identity and", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B028-004"], "canonical_claim": "Manifest objects retain `(namespace, mount-epoch, build-sequence)` identity and globally unique build identities, while loose mountpoint objects remain outside namespace ownership and unqualified.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-b-catalog.md#global-constraints"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2399", "topic": "The catalog has states Creating, Live, and Removing", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B028-011"], "canonical_claim": "The catalog has states `Creating`, `Live`, and `Removing`; each `CatalogEntry` contains a logical namespace, a random nonzero 128-bit incarnation, and a creator fence identity exactly when its state is `Creating`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-b-catalog.md#task-2"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2400", "topic": "RefCatalog is the token-CAS object at key cas/ref_catalog", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B028-012", "B043-039"], "canonical_claim": "`RefCatalog` is the token-CAS object at key `cas/ref_catalog`, with entries in canonical order by namespace bytes and no duplicate namespaces.; The namespace catalog is a token-CAS universe read as a cut; opaque 128-bit life ids in every key make removed-life debris inert and avoid physical-emptiness proofs for removal.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/how-we-got-here.md#turn-contiguous-chain", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-b-catalog.md#task-2"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2401", "topic": "Catalog admission independently requires encoded_catalog_bytes <= catalog_object_cap and", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B028-013"], "canonical_claim": "Catalog admission independently requires `encoded_catalog_bytes <= catalog_object_cap` and `fold_fixed_bytes + \u03a3 worst_case_entry_reservation <= fold_seal_object_cap`; equality is accepted, capacity overflow is loud, and removal is never refused.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-b-catalog.md#task-2"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2402", "topic": "Namespace creation consists of a token-CAS insertion of", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B028-014"], "canonical_claim": "Namespace creation consists of a token-CAS insertion of a `Creating` entry with a fresh incarnation and creator fence, creation of `<ns>/<inc>/_ckpt`, and a token-CAS transition from `Creating` to `Live` that rechecks the creator's admission generation and the observed catalog token.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-b-catalog.md#task-3"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2403", "topic": "The relink validator is a digest over the", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B029-079"], "canonical_claim": "The relink validator is a digest over the length-prefixed tuple `pool_uuid`, `disk_name`, `root_namespace`, `ref_name`, and `manifest_ref_text`; `root_namespace` alone does not identify a mount because same-`server_root_id` disks can share it.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-29-cas-relink-reoffer-redesign.md#wire-protocol"]}

